\f1\fs22 Sarah locked her office door and sat so fast at her desk, you\'92d think it was a sports car. She raced to warn Mr Fairy Boxers before the dark man with a particle pistol and ominous present-tense sentences, found him. She knew she should care nothing for a Cloudborne, especially a manual labourer, but there was no shaking the feeling she may have, in some indirect way, set the dark man on his trail. 
\f2\i What is this feeling? Is it guiltiness? No, 
\f1\i0 she decided. 
\f2\i It\'92s worse. It\'92s embarrassment.
\f1\i0 \
Sarah stroked her holoscreen with the grace of a poet. Let others deride it, dismiss it, and never suspect its capabilities. With a flick of her wrist, she spun a dizzying forest of three-dimensional business documents around her.  Beneath their canopy, she blinked a small console alive. From a drawer she produced a keyboard\'97yes, a keyboard!\'97and discreetly typed. Faster than the executive overviews around her could make an insomniac unconscious, she plunged deep inside office security, downloading surveillance logs and reconstituting half-overwritten image streams.\
Alas. Her glee, once as effervescent as champagne bubbles, fizzled into pursed-lipped disappointment. Nowhere in the scrambled data did she find a trace of the enigmatic dark man. There were no records of him lurking in reception; no record of his awkward marching in the hallway; no account of his reptilian slithering in Breezy Brains\'92 insufficiently sterile office. The particle pistol was absent, as was the aura of menace that accompanied it.\
Sarah ran the logs through image processors looking for editing artefacts. Nothing. The cold emptiness of the void left by the dark man's absence was now pregnant with Sarah's own dread.\
Manipulating security footage this way required sinister sophistication and stratospheric levels of authority, the kind which branded the dark man as a government agent, likely a spook from PAPER.\

\f2\i Tax me into poverty, 
\f1\i0 Sarah thought. 
\f2\i I sent this loon after Mr Fairy Boxers.
\f1\i0 \
